      ],
      "source": "https://ashfordtownhall.org/355/History",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town hosts Connecticut’s largest Boy Scout camp, June Norcross Webster, and Paul Newman's Hole in the Wall Gang Camp for children.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashford%2C_Connecticut",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Yale-Myers Forest spans Ashford, serving Yale School of Forestry research and sheltering the towering Ashford Oak, an eight‑meter‑circumference red oak.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashford%2C_Connecticut",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Mount Hope River runs north‑south through the town, while Bigelow Brook borders Eastford, and lakes like Ashford Lake and Lake Chaffee dot the landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashford%2C_Connecticut",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Natchaug and Nipmuck State Forests extend into Ashford, with the Natchaug and Nipmuck Trails winding through its forests.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashford%2C_Connecticut",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Joshua's Tract Conservation and Historic Trust protects several nature preserves across Ashford, safeguarding local wildlife and habitats.",
